  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Warm temperatures and breezy winds today. A\nchance of rain Downeast tonight through early Monday, then \nmostly across tHe north later Monday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure will exit across the Maritimes today. Breezy\nsouthwest winds around the exiting high will bring warmer \ntemperatures today. The remnants of Hurricane Isaias track \nsouth of the Gulf of Maine tonight through early Monday. The \nnorthern edge of the precipitation shield should clip Downeast \nareas tonight through early Monday. A cold front will then cross\nthe area Monday with a chance of rain across mostly \nnorthern/central areas.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...An area of precipitation will move through \nMonday night into Tuesday and bring a chance for light wintry \nprecipitation to central and northern parts of the forecast \narea.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nLow pressure across the Great Lakes will draw a warm front\ntoward the region Monday night through early Tuesday.\nOverrunning precipitation in advance of the warm front will\ndevelop across the region later Monday night through \nearly Tuesday. Precipitation should generally be in the form of\nrain. However, dependent on the onset time, just enough cold \nair could exist across northern areas and the Central Highlands\nto also support an interval of light snow later Monday night\nthrough early Tuesday. Little or no snow accumulation is \nexpected. The low approaches Tuesday, then crosses the region \nTuesday night with rain which could persist into early Wednesday.",
